meta {
  name: Export the paper
  type: http
  seq: 12
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/assessments/{{assessmentId}}/export?format=json
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

params:query {
  format: json
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.headers["content-disposition"]: contains attachment
}

docs {
  The whole paper as a file: every question with its answer, rubric, options, pairs,
  cognitive level, origin and the chunk ids it was written from. `format=md` returns
  the same paper as a document instead — questions first, answer key in its own
  section, so the first half can be printed for a room.

  **Guarded to the author, not to anyone who can see the row.** This body is the answer
  key. A sitter with a *released* result — who can legitimately read
  `public.question_key` for their own attempt — still gets 404 here, because being
  entitled to your own marked paper is not the same as being entitled to the paper.

  **No audit row.** An author reading `GET /assessments/{id}` is already handed every
  field in this file, so the export is a reformatting of a disclosure that has already
  happened rather than a new one. Auditing the download while leaving the screen
  unaudited would be theatre. The chat export makes the same call for the same reason.

  **The share token is deliberately absent from the body.** It is the whole access
  grant to the paper (DECISIONS.md D16), so it is a credential — and an export is a
  file that gets emailed, synced and forwarded. It stays on the review screen where it
  is visibly a link rather than one more field in a document. `tests/test_assessment_export.py`
  asserts it never appears in either format.

  Attempts are absent for a different reason: who sat the paper and what they scored is
  a document about other people, and it is not what "export the assessment" asks for.
  The gradebook is `GET /assessments/{id}/attempts`.

  `format` in the JSON is a version tag (`kitaably.assessment.v1`), so a future shape
  change is detectable by whatever was written against this one. Each question carries
  BOTH `format` (the shape) and `type` (the family that marks it) — an importer needs
  both, and one without the other cannot reconstruct the question (DECISIONS.md D25).
}
